  "helpGettingStarted": "Getting started",
  "helpGettingStarted1": "Put a record on your turntable, drop the needle and tap the microphone button. WaxClub listens for a few seconds, identifies the song and shows the lyrics in sync with the music.",
  "helpGettingStarted2": "Keep the phone close to the speakers and avoid talking near it while it listens.",
  "helpListening": "Listening and syncing",
  "helpListening1": "The first listen is quick (4 seconds); harder songs get up to 12 seconds automatically.",
  "helpListening2": "While a song plays, WaxClub checks the sync now and then through the microphone and corrects the timing.",
  "helpListening3": "At the end of each track it predicts the next one from the record's tracklist and confirms it by listening.",
  "helpFlipping": "Flipping the record",
  "helpFlipping1": "When a side ends, the button turns into \"Flip the record\". Tap it before or after you flip: the lyrics of the first track of the new side appear right away and start as soon as the needle hits the music.",
  "helpSpeed": "Turntable speed",
  "helpSpeed1": "Turntables rarely spin at exactly 33⅓ RPM. WaxClub measures your turntable's real speed while songs play and keeps the lyrics on time.",
  "helpSpeed2": "In the controls you can fine-tune the speed, reset it or lock it.",
  "helpTiming": "Lyrics running early or late",
  "helpTiming1": "Lyrics a few seconds off? Tap the line that is being sung: the lyrics jump to it on the phone and on the TV. While casting, the phone panel shows the previous, current and next lines to tap. For small corrections use −0.5 s / +0.5 s; the offset is remembered for that song (in Manual mode it moves the whole side).",
  "helpChangeRecord": "Change record and Discogs",
  "helpChangeRecord1": "Songs often appear on several records (albums, compilations, soundtracks). Tap the cover at the top left of the screen, then \"Change record\" to pick the exact record on your turntable; it becomes the default for those songs. Only vinyl records (LP and EP) are listed.",
  "helpChangeRecord2": "Tick \"Search Discogs\" to search the largest vinyl database. It is the same switch as the Discogs plugin (C1) in Plugins, where you also connect or disconnect your Discogs account. Your Discogs sign-in stays on this phone only.",
  "helpCollection": "Your collection",
  "helpCollection1": "Tap My Collection (the bookshelf button) to open your records. Add a record with the + button (it opens Identify), or tap the cover of the record that is playing and choose \"Add to collection\". The cloud button shows the sync with your WaxClub account and your Discogs connection.",
  "helpCollection2": "WaxClub counts how many times each record was played and when: any track heard counts the record once per listening session. Your collection and listening history are saved to your WaxClub account and sync between your phones. Open a record and tap Play to get it ready to play.",
  "helpTv": "Showing the lyrics on the TV",
  "helpTv1": "Tap the cast icon. Chromecast and Google TV devices appear automatically.",
  "helpTv2": "Fire TV: open the WaxClub app on the TV first; it appears in the list. If it does not, use \"Add by IP\" with the address shown on the TV.",
  "helpTv3": "Samsung, LG and other TVs without Chromecast: mirror your phone with Smart View, Cast or Wireless display (Miracast). WaxClub turns the TV into a second screen with only the lyrics, and the phone becomes the control panel.",
  "helpTv4": "The phone and the TV must be on the same Wi-Fi.",
  "helpTroubleshooting": "Troubleshooting",
  "helpTroubleshooting1": "Song not recognized: move the phone closer to the speakers and try again. Some rare records are not in the recognition catalog.",
  "helpTroubleshooting2": "Nothing is ever recognized: another app may be using the microphone (voice assistants, accessibility or call apps). WaxClub warns you when this happens. Close that app and try again.",
  "helpTroubleshooting3": "TV not found: check that it is on and on the same Wi-Fi, and tap \"Search again\". After a TV update it may take a few minutes to show up again.",
