  "helpPlugins": "Plugins (jukebox)",
  "helpPlugins1": "Tap Plugins (the jack plug button) to open the Plugin Jukebox. Each plugin is a colored 7\" single: green for languages, cyan for display, lilac for AI and orange for connections to other services (C1 Discogs comes preinstalled). English comes preinstalled; other languages will be available on the official WaxClub website.",
  "helpPlugins2": "Tap a record or type its code (e.g. L1) on the keypad and press Select to see details and turn it on or off. Records on the platter are the ones in use; the ones in the crate are coming soon.",
  "plugins": "Plugins",
  "camera": "Identify",
  "helpTopBar": "The top bar",
  "helpTopBar1": "At the top left is the WaxClub logo, or the cover of the record that is playing. With nothing playing, tap the logo to pick a record to play: type an artist and/or album, your collection comes first, then Discogs. While a record plays, tap the cover to see the tracklist. With the phone sideways, the record name, the song and what comes next appear beside it.",
  "helpTopBar2": "Below the top bar, on the right, the wooden buttons from left to right: Profile (user), Identify (camera), Manual (on/off switch), My Collection (bookshelf), Plugins (jack plug) and Help (question mark). Their names show up one by one when the app opens. The button at the top right shows the lyrics on your TV.",
  "manual": "Manual",
  "manualOnHint": "Manual mode on. Tap ▶ to choose where the needle starts; the lyrics follow the track timing. The switch turns off by itself when the record ends.",
  "manualOffHint": "Manual mode off: WaxClub recognizes the songs automatically.",
  "helpManual": "Manual mode",
  "helpManual1": "For records the recognition system does not know. With the Manual switch on, the microphone button becomes a chrome ▶: tap it, pick the track where the needle starts and drop the needle. The microphone only measures the volume to find the start; then the lyrics and track changes follow the record's track timing.",
  "helpManual2": "At the end of a side, flip the record and tap ▶. In the tracklist you can tap a track to jump to it. After Identify, WaxClub checks the recognition system and turns Manual mode on by itself when the record is not there. The switch starts off and turns off when the record ends (last song of the last side).",
